The findings reveal different kinds of signal. Billing has the largest adjusted negative rating association, while waiting appears negatively in about three times as many accounts. Safety concerns usually appear in low-rated feedback alongside other complaints. Positive descriptions of bedside manner provide a substantial body of experiences to learn from and preserve.
These results use 196,183 labeled Google reviews from 2019 to early June 2026, covering 9,904 U.S. healthcare listings. They describe self-selected public feedback; the model-generated labels remain provisional pending human validation. A listing may represent a hospital, clinic, emergency department or another service. Counts refer to accounts, rather than distinct patients or verified incidents.

